WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.560
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 marks the first
big-screen incarnation of Marvel Comics character

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:09.660
Mantis, played by Korean-French actress Pom
Klementieff.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.410
While she was relatively unknown before landing
her big break in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.199
there's still a chance you might have seen
Klementieff before.

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:19.859
Here's why Mantis may have looked familiar.

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:20.859
Early years

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:25.759
Klementieff got her start on camera fresh
out of drama school in independent French

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:26.759
films.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:31.190
Her first starring gig was in 2009's Wolf
as a Siberian reindeer herder.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.940
She followed it up with smaller roles over
the next few years in a wide variety of releases,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:41.140
including a string of parts in 2011, with
appearances in action thriller Sleepless Night

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.800
and crime comedy Borderline, just to name
a few …

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:57.980
Klementieff also appeared in 2012 gross out
comedy Porn in the Hood, the most profitable

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.920
French film of the year.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:00.920
Oldboy

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:05.890
Before landing the role of Mantis, Klementieff's
highest-profile performance by far was as

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:12.610
a bodyguard in Spike Lee's 2013 remake of
the 2003 South Korean thriller Oldboy, a very

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.020
physical role that required intense training.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.950
A fan of the original Oldboy, she wanted to
make sure the fight scenes were up to snuff,

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.940
and endured a strict regimen to prepare …

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:27.070
"I spent two months in New Orleans training
martial arts for three hours a day for two

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.070
months, yeah."

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:32.119
"As I said, I lost a toenail, but after the
end of the movie, because I'm a professional."

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:33.470
Hacker's Game

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:38.000
After breaking out with Oldboy, Klementieff
landed a starring role in the widely panned

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.630
2015 mid-budget romantic thriller Hacker's
Game, a high-stakes relationship drama between

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:45.250
two high-level hackers.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:50.740
Klementieff plays Loise, officially a cyber-detective
who falls for an Edward Snowden-like figure

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.950
"How did my files end up on your computer?"

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.640
"Who are you spying on, her or me?"

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.000
"I'm just trying to save that nice ass of
yours."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.439
The first film of Klementieff's to give the
actress top billing was also her first major

00:02:04.439 --> 00:02:09.660
misstep, with the Los Angeles Times in particular
throwing some serious shade her way, saying

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.560
she displayed "the acting range of a petulant
child."

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.680
"What are we doing?"

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.040
Sundance star

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.640
If you were fortunate enough to attend the
2017 Sundance Film Festival, you may have

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.700
seen Klementieff on a few panels and in two
supporting roles in films making their debut:

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:31.240
the social media dating drama Newness … and
the social media stalking comedy Ingrid Goes

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.230
West, starring Aubrey Plaza, which hits theaters
in August.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.410
A look ahead

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.220
We already know Klementieff will be back in
2018's Avengers: Infinity War, which brings

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.120
the Guardians face to face with the Avengers,
and James Gunn hinted in a Facebook post that

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:51.360
she would be back for confirmed sequel Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3, as well, saying his

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.170
love for Mantis and her fellow Guardians "goes
deeper than you guys can possibly imagine."

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.070
You can just feel the love ...

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.060
"You feel...

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:00.060
sexual love."

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:00.640
"No, no I don't."

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:01.640
"For her!"

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.060
Thanks for watching!

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.170
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

